.TH sandogasa-hattrack 1  sandogasa "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
sandogasa\-hattrack \- Look up a Fedora contributor\*(Aqs activity across services
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsandogasa\-hattrack\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-tz\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-working\-hours\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-holidays\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-holidays\fR] [\fB\-\-now\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Look up a Fedora contributor\*(Aqs activity across services
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\-source\fR \fI<TZ_SOURCE>\fR [default: auto]
Source for tzdb\*(Aqs zone1970.tab (country lookup table). `auto` picks the newer of system + bundled
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
system
.IP \(bu 2
bundled
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Colorize output. `auto` = TTY + NO_COLOR\-aware
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Auto\-detect: enable on a TTY when `NO_COLOR` is unset
.IP \(bu 2
always: Force colored output even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Disable colored output entirely
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-working\-hours\fR \fI<WORKING_HOURS>\fR [default: 9\-18]
Working\-hours range `START\-END` (24h local). Outside is dimmed
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-holidays\fR
Skip the Nager.Date public\-holiday lookup
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-holidays\fR
Force\-refetch holiday data from Nager.Date even when a cached copy is present
.TP
\fB\-\-now\fR \fI<NOW>\fR
Override "now" used for local\-time / holiday lookups. Accepts `YYYY\-MM\-DD` (midnight UTC) or full RFC 3339 (e.g. `2026\-03\-17T10:00:00Z`). For testing / demos
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
